WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.880
The plum pudding model of an atom

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.540
was one of the most widely accepted models

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:10.760
all over the world

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:13.780
for understanding the structure of the atom!

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:14.660
However,

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:17.280
several experiments performed by scientists

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:19.260
to study the atomic structure

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:22.220
showed astonishingly different results.

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:25.480
They were contradicting the plum pudding model.

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:27.280
This led many scientists

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:30.560
all over the globe to reconsider the structure of an atom

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:32.760
and study it again.

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:35.220
Around the year nineteen hundred and eleven,

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:37.780
a British physicist Ernst Rutherford,

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:40.980
carried out the famous Gold foil experiment.

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:44.540
He did this to understand the structure of an atom!

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:47.800
The experiment was carried out by Rutherford along with

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:50.840
Hans Geiger and Ernest Marsden.

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:52.380
The experiment he performed

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:54.660
was a breakthrough in the field of chemistry

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:57.280
which helped him understand the structure of an atom

00:00:57.380 --> 00:00:59.600
in a more accurate manner.

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:03.060
This is how the setup of his experiment looked like!

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:04.760
As we can see here,

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:07.020
he used a source of alpha particles,

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:10.440
locked in a lead container with a very small slit.

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:12.760
This ensured that the alpha particles

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:14.980
only came out through a small opening

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:17.500
and travelled in a straight line.

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:21.460
But why did he select alpha particles in the first place?

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:24.320
Well the alpha particles were having high energy

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:26.520
and were heavier as well.

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:28.320
So if we say the atom is like a

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:30.620
pudding of positively charged particles

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:32.980
with electrons embedded in it,

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:36.380
then the particles will pass straight through it.

00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:39.040
This is obvious because the heavier particles

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:41.060
will pierce through the lighter pudding structure

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:43.980
of the atom and pass through it.

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:46.400
This is what Rutherford thought!

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:47.600
For this reason,

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:50.720
their greater mass and energy compared to the protons

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:54.160
made him choose alpha particles for the experiment.

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:56.720
Next he used a very thin gold foil

00:01:56.820 --> 00:01:59.940
on which the alpha particles would bombard.

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:02.500
Why did he choose a gold foil?

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:03.180
Well,

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:06.220
a really thin gold foil was estimated to contain

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:08.860
approximately one thousand atoms.

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:10.080
Lesser the atoms,

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:12.900
more convenient the experiment would be!

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:13.740
Lastly,

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:17.380
are we able to locate this circular band with a gap here?

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:18.980
What could this be?

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:19.560
Well,

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:20.820
this is a screen.

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:22.040
A fluorescent screen

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:24.840
that would help us detect the radiation.

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:25.740
That means,

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:28.420
the screen will glow or emit fluorescent light

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:31.040
whenever alpha particles will hit it.

00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:35.220
So this is how the track of alpha particles can be traced.

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:36.800
Now we are all set to understand

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:38.780
how the experiment worked!

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:41.480
The alpha particles were emitted from the element

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:43.360
present in this box.

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:45.940
These directly hit the gold foil!

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:48.360
Now what should happen ideally?

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:50.880
As we know, the Thomson’s model suggested

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:53.460
that an atom is a sphere of positive charge

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:56.720
with negative electrons embedded inside it.

00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:59.600
That means it is expected that the alpha particles

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:01.500
will pass right through the atoms

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:03.720
and hit the detector straight!

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:05.240
And why so?

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:07.120
Because the mass of alpha particles

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:10.260
is heavier than the mass of positive charges.

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:13.040
That means they should directly hit the atom

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:15.280
and move ahead, through it.

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:17.580
Only a very small deviation

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:21.060
would probably be acceptable in this case.

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:23.220
But is this what he observed?

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:24.360
Not really,

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:27.820
he was astonished to get unexpected results!

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:30.020
What results did he get?

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:33.280
He found that most of the fast moving alpha particles

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:37.040
passed straight through the foil and hit the detector.

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:37.920
However,

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:41.700
some particles got deflected by small angles.

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:44.260
And lastly to his astonishment,

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:47.180
few alpha particles also rebounded.

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:49.560
Now how can this be possible?

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:52.220
These three observations made Rutherford think

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:55.520
that the plum pudding model is not really correct.

00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:57.420
Based on the conclusions he had,

00:03:57.480 --> 00:03:59.400
he put forward the new hypothesis

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:02.040
explaining the structure of atoms!

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:04.240
What were his conclusions?

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:07.040
Let us have a look at the conclusions by Rutherford

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:09.700
followed by the new atomic model put forth by him

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:11.140
in the next video!

